Feature: Captains for Towers
  The league also makes better [[captain]]s for [[Towers]]. A captain is the computer in the
  seat of a team: it reads the map of its team, with the [[fog]], and gives each drone an
  order once a second. Its numbers are its tuning: how long a drone stays in a fight that it
  loses, how long it then stays away, and how near an enemy must come before a held tower is
  defended. A Claude engineer can also change its code, in `commander.rs`.

  Use `--game captain` with the commands of the league. The league keeps the captains in the
  folder `league/captain`.

  In the fast arena, the drones fly their orders on their own: they take off from their base,
  turn as a T1-S turns, and circle a tower 40 m from it. The wind and the delay of each order
  change from seed to seed. The real referee of Towers runs the game.

  A challenger captain plays the champion twice on each seed: once as Blue, and once as Red.
  Thus a side that is better than the other does not help it. Its score in a game is +1 for a
  win, -1 for a loss and 0 for a draw, plus the points that it scored more than the other
  team, over 500.

  A captain that the Claude engineer changes in code plays as a process of its own, built from
  its own code. The champion plays with its own code. A change to the rules, the referee or the
  fog of Towers is refused.

  Expectation: A captain game in the fast arena is a game of Towers
    When the arena plays a game of Towers between two default captains
    Then the drones that flew in the captain game are 6
    And the captain game is won by Blue or won by Red or a draw

  Expectation: A captain playing itself from both sides scores nothing
    When the default captain plays itself from both sides
    Then the score of the captain against itself is 0

  Expectation: A captain that is better from both sides becomes the champion
    Given the champion captain is the timid captain
    And the challenger captain is the default captain
    When the league judges the captain challenger
    Then the verdict is promoted

  Expectation: A captain that is worse stays out
    Given the champion captain is the default captain
    And the challenger captain is the timid captain
    When the league judges the captain challenger
    Then the verdict is kept out

  Expectation: A captain changed in code plays with its own code
    If the challenger played with the code of the champion, the two would be the same captain,
    and the difference would be exactly 0.

    When a Claude strategy gives a captain whose code sends every drone home
    Then the mean difference of the captain challenger is below 0
    And the verdict is kept out

  Expectation: A captain that changes the referee stays out
    When a Claude strategy gives a captain that changes the referee
    Then the verdict is refused
    And the reason is it changes the rules
